  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**  \n   Coordinate-wise optimization via convex subproblems for each variable, leveraging the convexity of the max correlation objective in each variable. This approach iteratively refines each h[i] to minimize its contribution to the maximum overlap, ensuring feasibility through projections. It addresses the high dimensionality and non-convexity by decomposing the problem and using efficient line searches.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**  \n   - **Variables**: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, n = n_points, with each h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h[i] = n/2.  \n   - **Objective**: Minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u2211_{x=0}^{2n-1} h[x](1 - h[(x+k) % n]) * (2/n).  \n   - **Constraints**: Sum constraint \u2211h[i] = n/2 and bounds 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.  \n   - **Convexity**: For fixed h[j], j \u2260 i, the max correlation is convex in h[i], enabling ternary search.  \n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**  \n   a. **Initialization**:  \n      - Use initial_h_values if available, else create a uniform vector.  \n      - Ensure sum(h) = n/2 via scaling.  \n   b. **Precompute Correlations**:  \n      - Compute the full correlation matrix for initial h.  \n   c. **Coordinate-wise Update Loop**:  \n      1. For each h[i]:  \n         - Fix other variables, compute affected correlation terms.  \n         - Perform ternary search on h[i] \u2208 [0,1] to minimize max correlation.  \n         - Update h[i] and adjust correlations for affected shifts.  \n      2. After each cycle:  \n         - Clip h to [0,1].  \n         - Scale h to meet sum constraint.  \n   d. **Termination**:  \n      - Stop after budget exhaustion or no improvement for multiple cycles.  \n   e. **Return Best Solution**:  \n      - Return h with smallest C\u2085 found, ensuring feasibility.  \n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**  \n   - **Resolution**: Use n_points = 256 for balance between accuracy and speed.  \n   - **Termination**: Check improvement every 50 cycles, stopping if \u0394C\u2085 < 1e-5.  \n   - **Ternary Search**: Use 10 iterations per h[i] for precision.  \n   - **Fallback**: Retain initial_h_values if no feasible improvement found.  \n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**  \n   - **Time Estimate**: ~1100s for 200 cycles with n=256, efficient correlation updates.  \n   - **Numerical Stability**: Use precise floating-point arithmetic, validate feasibility at each step.  \n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**  \n   - Check sum(h) = n/2 \u00b1 1e-6 and h[i] \u2208 [0,1].  \n   - Recompute C\u2085 via evaluation function and verify against stored minimum.  \n   - Return h and C\u2085 only if they meet all constraints.",
